      "start_seconds": 0.72,
      "end_seconds": 2.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "afternoon thanks for coming in"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.76,
      "end_seconds": 6.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "hello thanks for fitting me in"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.14,
      "end_seconds": 11.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "sorry about the wait, we're running a bit behind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.73,
      "end_seconds": 18.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "oh that's fine. I was just reading something on my phone"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.38,
      "end_seconds": 22.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "what's the main thing today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.1,
      "end_seconds": 29.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Well, I've been having a sudden severe tummy pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.2,
      "end_seconds": 33.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "how long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.71,
      "end_seconds": 44.23,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "It's been like this since last Tuesday. Work has been very busy so so I kept ignoring it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.39,
      "end_seconds": 54.3,
      "duration_seconds": 8.91,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.73,
      "end_seconds": 60.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Honestly, every other day. I notice it more with movement."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.72,
      "end_seconds": 63.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.85,
      "end_seconds": 75.99,
      "duration_seconds": 11.14,
      "text": "Shoulder tip pain goes along with it, most of the time. Ah, uh, the Shoulder tip pain? That's been for six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.82,
      "end_seconds": 96.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "a few quick ones: fever, blood in the vomit or diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.84,
      "end_seconds": 99.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "nope, nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.6,
      "end_seconds": 104.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.28,
      "end_seconds": 107.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.12,
      "end_seconds": 113.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.74,
      "end_seconds": 116.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "I have migraines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.05,
      "end_seconds": 121.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Before we go further any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.97,
      "end_seconds": 131.8,
      "duration_seconds": 8.83,
      "text": "Yes, grass pollen. I've no idea what the reaction was, only that I'm not supposed to have it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.32,
      "end_seconds": 136.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Alright, what do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.14,
      "end_seconds": 141.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.52,
      "end_seconds": 144.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.69,
      "end_seconds": 148.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.66,
      "end_seconds": 163.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "alright, tell me your medicines, please"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.76,
      "end_seconds": 172.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "it's sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed. Ibuprofen, 600 milligrams, three times a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.77,
      "end_seconds": 191.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.8,
      "end_seconds": 197.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "I had a varicose vein procedure last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.82,
      "end_seconds": 202.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.0,
      "end_seconds": 218.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.79,
      "end_seconds": 250.51,
      "duration_seconds": 12.72,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.5 degrees BP is 135 over 83. And pulse is 108 beats a minute oxygen saturation is 96 percent respiratory rate 20."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.3,
      "end_seconds": 254.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "is that alright, you know, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.18,
      "end_seconds": 262.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.79,
      "end_seconds": 267.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "right, let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.67,
      "end_seconds": 270.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Does that that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.32,
      "end_seconds": 286.76,
      "duration_seconds": 8.44,
      "text": "your tummy is rigid like a board and very tender everywhere, and you are lying completely still"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.31,
      "end_seconds": 292.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "all finished thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.77,
      "end_seconds": 318.67,
      "duration_seconds": 12.9,
      "text": "from what you've told me and and what I found, this is probably a perforated stomach ulcer i want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.87,
      "end_seconds": 323.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.0,
      "end_seconds": 347.42,
      "duration_seconds": 22.42,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a perforated stomach ulcer, but I'd like to confirm. I'll request a CT scan, it'll help with possible perforation. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'd like to arrange urgent blood tests for acute abdomen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.33,
      "end_seconds": 352.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "um where would I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.14,
      "end_seconds": 372.69,
      "duration_seconds": 18.55,
      "text": "nothing to eat or drink you need an operation urgently. The surgical team would be the right next step I'll refer you. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens go to emergency. Let's plan a check straight away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.09,
      "end_seconds": 378.79,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.62,
      "end_seconds": 384.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "I think we're done unless you have questions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.99,
      "end_seconds": 388.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks"
    }
  ]
